{{fbdoc item="title" value="BASS"}}----
Audio library for sample, stream and tracker-module playback and recording.

Website: https://www.un4seen.com/bass.html
Platforms supported: Windows, Linux
Headers to include: bass.bi
Header version: 2.4.14
Examples: in examples/sound/BASS/

The binding's sample and stream API has been checked with native BASS 2.4.18.3 on 32-bit and 64-bit Windows and 64-bit Linux. Use a library matching the executable's architecture. Windows needs the BASS DLL and an import library compatible with the compiler's declarations; the FreeBASIC binding uses ##Extern "Windows-MS"##. The supplied C import archive and a FreeBASIC import archive may therefore use different linker names for the same DLL functions.

Compare ##HiWord(BASS_GetVersion())## with ##BASSVERSION## before using the 2.4 API. Handles and ##DWORD## fields are 32-bit values even in a 64-bit application; ##QWORD## byte positions are 64-bit. Check each load or playback result and release the process's handles with ##BASS_Free()##. Newer SDKs reserve the older ##BASS_INFO## hardware-capability fields; their names remain in this binding for source compatibility.

The example accepts an optional module filename, using the package's ##dne_trtn.mod## relative to the executable when none is supplied. The sound-folder examples accept a data directory containing their media files. Setting ##FB_EXAMPLE_AUTOPLAY## enables bounded playback checks; otherwise the programs retain their interactive controls. The demonstration exercises stream/sample playback, pause/resume, restart and volume controls in that mode. BASSMOD is a separate library with its own binding.

Linux amd64 qualification includes five media formats, independent C/FreeBASIC PCM comparisons and all three original clients on both backends. On the container without a sound card, the clients use ALSA's official null PCM through a process-local ##ALSA_CONFIG_PATH##. This exercises genuine BASS/ALSA output while discarding samples; physical sound-card operation remains a separate check.

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}
{{fbdoc item="filename" value="examples/manual/libraries/bass.bas"}}%%(freebasic)
'' examples/manual/libraries/bass.bas
''
'' Example extracted from the FreeBASIC Manual
'' from topic 'BASS'
'' Purpose: Play a tracker module through the native BASS output device.
'' Responsibilities: Asset paths, playback errors and owned resource cleanup.
'' This example contains no network streaming or recording.
''
'' See Also: https://www.freebasic.net/wiki/wikka.php?wakka=ExtLibbass
'' --------

#include Once "bass.bi"

'' An optional filename also allows running the executable outside this tree.
Dim As String sound_file = Command(1)
If sound_file = "" Then sound_file = ExePath() & "/../../sound/data/dne_trtn.mod"

If (HiWord(BASS_GetVersion()) <> BASSVERSION) Then
	Print "BASS 2.4 required!"
	End 1
End If

If (BASS_Init(-1, 44100, 0, 0, 0) = 0) Then
	Print "Could not initialize BASS"
	End 1
End If

Dim As HMUSIC test = BASS_MusicLoad(False, StrPtr(sound_file), 0, 0, BASS_MUSIC_LOOP, 0)
If (test = 0) Then
	Print "BASS could not load '" & sound_file & "'"
	BASS_Free()
	End 1
End If

If BASS_ChannelPlay(test, False) = 0 Then
	Print "BASS could not start playback: "; BASS_ErrorGetCode()
	BASS_Free()
	End 1
End If

If( Environ( "FB_EXAMPLE_AUTOPLAY" ) <> "" ) Then
	Sleep 1500, 1
	Dim As QWORD position = BASS_ChannelGetPosition(test, BASS_POS_BYTE)
	If position = Cast(QWORD, -1) OrElse position = 0 Then
		BASS_Free()
		End 1
	End If
	Print "BASS position seconds:"; BASS_ChannelBytes2Seconds(test, position)
Else
	Print "Sound playing; waiting to keypress to stop and exit..."
	Sleep
End If

If BASS_ChannelStop(test) = 0 Then
	BASS_Free()
	End 1
End If
If BASS_MusicFree(test) = 0 Then
	BASS_Free()
	End 1
End If
If BASS_Free() = 0 Then End 1
'' end of bass.bas
%%

